BANKWISE DEMO BANK
ATM SERVICES GUIDE

1. INTRODUCTION

An Automated Teller Machine (ATM) allows customers to perform basic banking services without visiting a bank branch. Depending on the bank and ATM, customers may be able to withdraw cash, check balances, print mini statements, and access card-related services.

This is a fictional/demo document created for the BankWise AI RAG project. It is not an official banking policy.

2. CASH WITHDRAWAL

Customers can use an eligible debit card at a supported ATM to withdraw cash.

General steps:
• Insert or tap the card if supported.
• Select the required language.
• Enter the required authentication information privately.
• Select Cash Withdrawal.
• Enter the required amount.
• Collect the cash and card.
• Take the receipt if required.

Customers should always verify that the transaction has been completed successfully.

3. BALANCE ENQUIRY

An ATM may provide a balance enquiry option. Customers can select this service and follow the instructions displayed on the ATM screen.

The available balance shown may depend on the bank's system and transaction processing status.

4. MINI STATEMENT

Some ATMs provide a mini statement showing recent account transactions.

The number of transactions displayed and the availability of this feature may vary between banks and ATM machines.

5. ATM WITHDRAWAL LIMIT

Banks may set daily or transaction-level limits for ATM cash withdrawals.

The applicable limit can depend on:
• Account type
• Debit card type
• Customer settings
• Bank policy
• ATM network

Customers should check the current limit through their bank's official channels.

6. FAILED CASH WITHDRAWAL

Sometimes an ATM transaction may fail.

If the account is debited but cash is not received, the customer should:
• Keep the transaction details.
• Check the transaction status through the official banking application or website.
• Contact the bank through an official support channel if the issue remains unresolved.

Customers should never share confidential authentication information while reporting the problem.

7. ATM CARD RETENTION

An ATM may occasionally retain a card because of technical problems or other reasons.

If this happens, the customer should:
• Contact the bank through its official support channel.
• Follow the bank's card-retrieval or replacement procedure.
• Never provide the card PIN to another person.

8. LOST OR STOLEN DEBIT CARD

If a debit card is lost or stolen, the customer should report it immediately through an official banking channel.

Possible official channels include:
• Bank mobile application
• Internet banking
• Official bank helpline
• Bank branch

The customer should follow the bank's procedure for blocking or replacing the card.

9. ATM SAFETY

Customers should follow basic ATM safety practices:
• Keep the PIN confidential.
• Cover the keypad while entering authentication information.
• Avoid accepting assistance from unknown people.
• Check the ATM for anything unusual before using it.
• Collect the card and cash before leaving.
• Keep ATM receipts secure when they contain sensitive information.

10. SUSPICIOUS ATM ACTIVITY

If a customer notices suspicious activity around an ATM or discovers an unfamiliar transaction, they should leave the area if necessary and contact the bank through an official support channel.

Customers should not confront suspicious individuals.

11. ATM TRANSACTION RECEIPTS

ATM receipts may contain transaction information. Customers should keep them secure and dispose of unwanted receipts carefully.

Customers should avoid sharing transaction receipts publicly if they contain sensitive information.

12. ATM SERVICE AVAILABILITY

ATM services may sometimes be unavailable because of maintenance, network problems, cash availability, or technical issues.

Customers can try another authorized ATM or contact the bank through an official channel.

13. IMPORTANT SECURITY INFORMATION

Never share:
• ATM PIN
• OTP
• UPI PIN
• Internet banking password
• CVV
• Full card credentials
• Other authentication information

Bank staff should not ask customers to disclose confidential authentication credentials.

14. BANKWISE AI LIMITATION

BankWise AI is an informational chatbot created for a demonstration RAG project.

It cannot:
• Access real bank accounts
• Check real account balances
• Withdraw money
• Perform ATM transactions
• Block a real card
• Transfer money
• Access customer credentials

For real banking problems, customers should contact their actual bank through an official channel.

DISCLAIMER

ATM features, withdrawal limits, fees, availability, and procedures may vary between banks and may change over time. Always verify current information through the relevant bank's official channels.
